WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:01:47.357 --> 00:01:48.692
No life forms...

3
00:01:50.694 --> 00:01:51.862
and not a lot of water.

4
00:01:52.446 --> 00:01:55.199
Weird place to build a Second Foundation.

5
00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.658
Well. you would say that.

6
00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.119
Planetfall in four.

7
00:02:00.037 --> 00:02:01.871
So you're saying we have four minutes

8
00:02:01.872 --> 00:02:04.208
to talk about
what we haven't been talking about?

9
00:02:04.209 --> 00:02:05.918
Buckle up. It's gonna be a bumpy EDL.

10
00:02:05.919 --> 00:02:07.084
Salvor.

11
00:02:07.085 --> 00:02:09.085
You told me. all right? You've said it.

12
00:02:09.086 --> 00:02:11.672
Every bad dream you've ever had
has come true.

13
00:02:11.673 --> 00:02:14.843
That doesn't mean that this one will.
I have to believe that we can change this.

14
00:02:15.344 --> 00:02:16.428
But you don't.

15
00:02:17.304 --> 00:02:18.514
You don't believe that.

16
00:02:20.557 --> 00:02:25.521
150 years from now. I die on a battlefield
trying to save humanity.

17
00:02:25.522 --> 00:02:28.190
- It's better than a sickbed.
- You can't just brush this off.

18
00:02:28.191 --> 00:02:30.233
And I guess it means
I won't die any sooner. right?

19
00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:33.153
- I've never felt so alive.
- You could get in a cryo-pod.

20
00:02:33.154 --> 00:02:34.946
Right now. go back to Terminus.

21
00:02:34.947 --> 00:02:38.450
And still end up on the battlefield
at our distant turning point.

22
00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:44.206
After all. there may be infinite ways
to arrive at the inevitable.

23
00:02:44.207 --> 00:02:46.437
<i>Warning. planetary surface thin.</i>

24
00:02:46.438 --> 00:02:48.668
<i>Landing site unstable.</i>

25
00:02:48.669 --> 00:02:50.337
Well. we got no choice. <i>Beggar</i>.

26
00:02:52.631 --> 00:02:56.593
- You're steering?
- Yes. I have control. Brace yourselves.

27
00:02:57.511 --> 00:02:58.720
I'll set us down.

28
00:03:33.714 --> 00:03:35.027
This is Ignis?

29
00:03:35.028 --> 00:03:36.341
Abandoned mines?

30
00:03:39.386 --> 00:03:40.762
We're not on Ignis.

31
00:03:43.557 --> 00:03:45.391
Well. then where the fuck are we?

32
00:03:45.392 --> 00:03:47.894
Oona's World. an imperial mining site.

33
00:03:47.895 --> 00:03:51.064
until its minerals were exhausted
3.000 years ago.

34
00:03:51.065 --> 00:03:52.940
Currently uninhabited.

35
00:03:52.941 --> 00:03:57.237
Hari. you agreed Ignis was crucial
for the Second Foundation.

36
00:03:57.238 --> 00:03:59.406
It is. So is this.

37
00:03:59.407 --> 00:04:00.532
Since when?

38
00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.951
Since the Radiant required it.

39
00:04:02.952 --> 00:04:04.702
I know how the math works.

40
00:04:04.703 --> 00:04:06.747
It doesn't design travel itineraries.

41
00:04:06.748 --> 00:04:07.915
It does now.

42
00:04:08.624 --> 00:04:11.793
There's a place in those mountains.
about 500 meters from here.

43
00:04:11.794 --> 00:04:13.461
which it requires me to visit.

44
00:04:13.462 --> 00:04:18.090
Hari. the model is adaptive.
not omniscient.

45
00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:20.927
You wanna go out there.
you can fucking do it alone!

46
00:04:20.928 --> 00:04:24.932
I'm a projection. Gaal.
bound by whatever network is nearest.

47
00:04:24.933 --> 00:04:27.267
I can transfer myself back
into the Radiant.

48
00:04:27.268 --> 00:04:29.602
but I need one of you to carry it for me.

49
00:04:29.603 --> 00:04:32.855
I will not trust you
on something I can't verify.

50
00:04:32.856 --> 00:04:35.692
And I'm not relinquishing control
of the <i>Beggar</i> until this is done.

51
00:04:35.693 --> 00:04:37.360
Just go with him. Gaal.

52
00:04:37.361 --> 00:04:41.782
No. You want me to carry you around
like a rat in a handbag.

53
00:04:41.783 --> 00:04:43.575
- I won't do it. Hari. This...
- Hey!

54
00:04:48.747 --> 00:04:49.747
Do it. Gaal.

55
00:04:49.748 --> 00:04:52.626
Take him with you.
so we can get the fuck out of here.

56
00:04:54.419 --> 00:04:56.505
They were called
the Monuments to Industry.

57
00:04:57.172 --> 00:04:59.216
We're gonna get a rare. close-up look.

58
00:05:00.425 --> 00:05:04.263
- Stay alert while we're gone.
- Why? The planet's uninhabited.

59
00:05:04.264 --> 00:05:06.557
Uninhabited doesn't mean we're alone.

60
00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:25.784
It's unthinkable to incinerate the warden.

61
00:05:26.535 --> 00:05:28.745
- It's barbaric.
- Maybe an error of some kind.

62
00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.373
The Vault is a device after all.

63
00:05:31.374 --> 00:05:32.457
No.

64
00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:37.129
The Vault is a man. and it's literally
made out of Hari Seldon.

65
00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:39.756
I told you he wouldn't approve of
what you've done here.

66
00:05:39.757 --> 00:05:42.217
You think this is divine judgment. Claric?

67
00:05:42.218 --> 00:05:44.595
No. but it was a judgment.

68
00:05:46.096 --> 00:05:47.305
Whatever the case.

69
00:05:47.306 --> 00:05:49.933
we don't have time to cry
and clasp our icons.

70
00:05:51.018 --> 00:05:56.148
How could Seldon's math foresee
someone specific. like Hober Mallow.

71
00:05:56.149 --> 00:05:59.192
who could even be born.
much less request his presence?

72
00:05:59.193 --> 00:06:02.237
We don't actually know
the Vault was making a request.

73
00:06:02.238 --> 00:06:04.238
- It could be a warning.
- Right.

74
00:06:04.239 --> 00:06:06.950
The last thing we should do
is allow that blood-poor son of a bitch

75
00:06:06.951 --> 00:06:09.161
- anywhere near the Vault.
- Don't be ridiculous.

76
00:06:09.162 --> 00:06:10.808
Of course we're finding Hober Mallow.

77
00:06:10.809 --> 00:06:12.945
And we're walking him into that Vault.

78
00:06:12.946 --> 00:06:15.082
Psychohistory isn't determinism. Poly.

79
00:06:15.083 --> 00:06:18.545
It's not a single path. but it is
a landscape that sometimes narrows

80
00:06:18.546 --> 00:06:21.632
into a dangerous mountain pass
that can't be avoided.

81
00:06:21.633 --> 00:06:24.217
That's why we call it a crisis.

82
00:06:24.218 --> 00:06:29.806
Seldon knew that in his first crisis
that success would require action.

83
00:06:29.807 --> 00:06:33.018
And the action we took
at that time had a name.

84
00:06:33.019 --> 00:06:34.143
{\an8}Salvor Hardin.

85
00:06:34.144 --> 00:06:37.773
{\an8}And if Hari Seldon had engraved the name
Salvor Hardin somewhere at that time.

86
00:06:37.774 --> 00:06:39.024
you'd have a point.

87
00:06:40.067 --> 00:06:41.068
Poly?

88
00:06:42.945 --> 00:06:43.946
No.

89
00:06:44.696 --> 00:06:47.491
So.
you think Hober Mallow is our new action?

90
00:06:47.492 --> 00:06:48.909
Look. I don't know why.

91
00:06:49.576 --> 00:06:53.163
But his name is on the only embodiment
we have right now of Seldon's Plans.

92
00:06:53.164 --> 00:06:54.643
You aren't even a believer.

93
00:06:54.644 --> 00:06:56.123
I believe in psychohistory.

94
00:06:56.124 --> 00:06:58.668
I believe
that the Empire is going to fall.

95
00:06:58.669 --> 00:07:02.172
And if we're smart.
we're the ones to bring it down.

96
00:07:03.298 --> 00:07:07.010
Humans will wallow like beasts
for a very long time.

97
00:07:07.011 --> 00:07:09.387
unless we use what Seldon gave us

98
00:07:09.388 --> 00:07:11.994
and walk through
that blasted mountain pass

99
00:07:11.995 --> 00:07:14.601
with that fucking asshole. Hober Mallow.

100
00:07:16.019 --> 00:07:17.271
Fine.

101
00:07:17.896 --> 00:07:19.022
Hober Mallow?

102
00:07:19.815 --> 00:07:23.297
Never heard that name before.
I wasn't even sure it's a person.

103
00:07:23.298 --> 00:07:26.780
Ask me. Mallow could be
a region of space or a species of nut.

104
00:07:26.781 --> 00:07:28.719
Arguably. he is a species of nut.

105
00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:30.658
He trained for the priesthood.

106
00:07:30.659 --> 00:07:32.910
but he was too much
for the Revered Fathers.

107
00:07:32.911 --> 00:07:37.708
Instead. he trailed my fellow
missionaries like a venereal disease.

108
00:07:37.709 --> 00:07:41.378
selling religious paraphernalia
and fake relics.

109
00:07:41.379 --> 00:07:45.131
He sold 38 of Seldon's finger bones

110
00:07:45.132 --> 00:07:47.509
before Foundation
revoked his trades license.

111
00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:49.887
Why would the Prophet ask
for a man like that?

112
00:07:49.888 --> 00:07:52.264
Seldon always appreciated a good joke.

113
00:07:52.265 --> 00:07:54.099
He was human too. you know?

114
00:07:54.725 --> 00:07:58.415
The Prophet's title was something
that we bestowed on him after.

115
00:07:58.416 --> 00:08:02.107
- So. where are we headed?
- According to my contacts. Korell.

116
00:08:02.108 --> 00:08:03.859
Out on the Whassalian Rift?

117
00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:06.152
Traders aren't even allowed there.

118
00:08:06.153 --> 00:08:10.324
You're talking about a man who views
any prohibition as a personal challenge.

119
00:08:10.325 --> 00:08:13.493
If it's forbidden. Hober traffics in it.

120
00:08:54.785 --> 00:08:55.786
What are they?

121
00:08:56.578 --> 00:08:58.247
Autonomous mining machines.

122
00:08:59.289 --> 00:09:01.458
They sucked the Palladium
from the pores of the planet.

123
00:09:01.459 --> 00:09:03.418
And then.
when there was nothing left of value.

124
00:09:03.419 --> 00:09:05.379
they were turned loose
upon the population.

125
00:09:07.422 --> 00:09:11.093
The Emperors are hollow men
who hollow out their worlds.

126
00:09:12.052 --> 00:09:13.469
How do you know all this?

127
00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:14.887
Why do you know all this?

128
00:09:14.888 --> 00:09:17.306
It's called psychohistory. Gaal.

129
00:09:17.307 --> 00:09:20.393
Hari. I can help you.
You just have to let me in.

130
00:09:20.394 --> 00:09:23.730
I'm the only other person in the galaxy
who can read the Radiant.

131
00:09:23.731 --> 00:09:25.858
Yes. but you're disruptive.

132
00:09:26.775 --> 00:09:28.360
Around and around we go.

133
00:09:29.111 --> 00:09:31.446
We're here at the Radiant's behest.

134
00:09:32.281 --> 00:09:35.200
It's not some detour keeping you
from what you want.

135
00:09:35.701 --> 00:09:37.327
What I want is to slap you.

136
00:09:38.036 --> 00:09:39.641
You tried that already.

137
00:09:39.642 --> 00:09:41.248
I'm talking about Salvor.

138
00:09:42.457 --> 00:09:44.376
You're dangling the prospects of hope.

139
00:09:45.294 --> 00:09:46.295
It's a mistake.

140
00:09:46.879 --> 00:09:49.631
The future you've seen
may very well be immutable.

141
00:09:50.132 --> 00:09:53.010
You were happy to get the word
"Ignis" from my vision and act on it.

142
00:09:53.011 --> 00:09:54.594
Now. if I do it. it's wrong?

143
00:09:54.595 --> 00:09:56.846
Here's the difference.
which you should already grasp.

144
00:09:56.847 --> 00:10:01.310
My Plan makes small changes in the present
to adjust large events in the future.

145
00:10:01.311 --> 00:10:04.271
You want to observe
one very small event in the future.

146
00:10:04.272 --> 00:10:06.564
the death of a specific human being.

147
00:10:06.565 --> 00:10:09.442
and apply massive forces in the present
to avert it.

148
00:10:09.443 --> 00:10:12.321
- Salvor solved your first crisis.
- She had help.

149
00:10:12.905 --> 00:10:14.780
Every historical condition
was on her side.

150
00:10:14.781 --> 00:10:16.950
If it hadn't been her.
it would have been someone else.

151
00:10:16.951 --> 00:10:18.034
Conditions?

152
00:10:18.035 --> 00:10:21.120
You didn't put any psychohistorians
on Terminus.

153
00:10:21.121 --> 00:10:24.333
- And if it wasn't for her ability...
- I intended one psychohistorian

154
00:10:24.334 --> 00:10:25.626
to be on Terminus!

155
00:10:26.335 --> 00:10:27.336
Right?

156
00:10:29.338 --> 00:10:30.506
In another life.

157
00:10:31.298 --> 00:10:34.009
you might have taught your daughter
all about my Vault.

158
00:10:35.511 --> 00:10:38.055
You seem to think
you're very indispensable.

159
00:10:38.056 --> 00:10:40.349
Well. Gaal. it is my Plan.

160
00:10:41.475 --> 00:10:45.145
But no. at enough scale.
I am insignificant.

161
00:11:05.374 --> 00:11:07.125
We weren't always alone in this.

162
00:11:08.502 --> 00:11:09.877
- What?
- You said earlier

163
00:11:09.878 --> 00:11:12.965
that you were the only other person
who could read the Radiant.

164
00:11:12.966 --> 00:11:14.716
That wasn't always the case.

165
00:11:16.218 --> 00:11:18.761
I had a life partner. Yanna.

166
00:11:18.762 --> 00:11:21.305
She helped me birth psychohistory.

167
00:11:21.306 --> 00:11:24.017
You could say it was the only child
we had together.

168
00:11:24.018 --> 00:11:26.019
The only one that survived anyway.

169
00:11:29.439 --> 00:11:31.149
I wouldn't finish that just yet.

170
00:11:31.817 --> 00:11:33.569
We still have a long way to go.

171
00:11:34.486 --> 00:11:35.904
You said 500 meters.

172
00:11:36.738 --> 00:11:38.031
Horizontally.

173
00:11:43.662 --> 00:11:46.081
I swear. Hari.
this had better be worth it.

174
00:11:46.082 --> 00:11:47.457
It will be.

175
00:11:48.667 --> 00:11:50.169
We're going to meet an old friend.

176
00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:51.253
An old friend?

177
00:12:48.602 --> 00:12:50.771
442. on your feet!

178
00:12:53.941 --> 00:12:55.067
Move it!

179
00:13:07.538 --> 00:13:08.539
No.

180
00:13:09.164 --> 00:13:12.208
713. hands off Prisoner 429.

181
00:13:12.209 --> 00:13:15.045
Just give him a minute.
He'll make the day.

182
00:13:21.885 --> 00:13:23.595
He wasn't being willful.

183
00:13:24.596 --> 00:13:26.849
He had more work left in him.

184
00:14:02.926 --> 00:14:03.927
Bel Riose.

185
00:14:04.595 --> 00:14:05.888
Lady Demerzel.

186
00:14:06.722 --> 00:14:08.055
I'm here with an offer.

187
00:14:08.056 --> 00:14:10.726
Empire needs the Hero of the 20th Fleet.

188
00:14:10.727 --> 00:14:12.227
There are battles to be fought.

189
00:14:14.605 --> 00:14:16.564
- Where?
- The Periphery.

190
00:14:16.565 --> 00:14:19.193
You'll start on Siwenna.
in the Normannic Sector.

191
00:14:19.194 --> 00:14:20.943
A new enemy has risen.

192
00:14:20.944 --> 00:14:22.863
Siwenna's a backwater dump.

193
00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:25.365
That's coming from someone who lives here.

194
00:14:26.158 --> 00:14:28.118
Complete the mission and go free.

195
00:14:30.078 --> 00:14:31.579
Why so generous?

196
00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:35.083
- Day had a notion you might refuse.
- Yeah. He's not wrong.

197
00:14:35.709 --> 00:14:38.586
His leadership is capricious and unwise.

198
00:14:38.587 --> 00:14:41.965
That puts you in a position
of strength then. doesn't it?

199
00:14:43.383 --> 00:14:44.635
Their freedom too.

200
00:14:46.011 --> 00:14:50.015
And just to be clear.
that's not my price to go with ya.

201
00:14:51.183 --> 00:14:54.060
It's my price to enter
into a conversation about it.

202
00:14:54.061 --> 00:14:58.023
You were sent to Lepsis because you
insisted on a safer path for your sailors.

203
00:14:58.774 --> 00:15:01.193
Do you wish to remain here
for a similar mistake?

204
00:15:01.194 --> 00:15:03.779
Freedom for them.

205
00:15:03.780 --> 00:15:05.113
Not freedom.

206
00:15:08.242 --> 00:15:11.912
Longer breaks. Better equipment.
Medical care.

207
00:15:18.168 --> 00:15:19.169
Fine.

208
00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:23.966
And now. we negotiate if I return or not.

209
00:15:26.593 --> 00:15:27.886
I'd need free rein.

210
00:15:28.554 --> 00:15:30.597
No countermanding from Empire.

211
00:15:30.598 --> 00:15:32.641
That was already the plan.

212
00:15:33.225 --> 00:15:34.392
Follow me.

213
00:15:34.393 --> 00:15:40.065
Tell Empire he can go fuck himself
in his big. blue fucking dress.

214
00:15:42.651 --> 00:15:45.112
I have an order to carry out
if you say no.

215
00:15:46.572 --> 00:15:48.198
I ain't afraid to die.

216
00:15:49.116 --> 00:15:50.450
That's why we want you.

217
00:15:52.828 --> 00:15:55.414
And I have a way to make it worthwhile
to say yes.

218
00:15:57.374 --> 00:15:58.834
Glawen Curr.

219
00:16:05.632 --> 00:16:12.347
Empire executed my husband six years ago.

220
00:16:12.973 --> 00:16:14.849
You were told he was executed.

221
00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:16.727
It was part of the punishment.

222
00:16:21.064 --> 00:16:22.524
I don't believe you.

223
00:16:23.609 --> 00:16:24.984
Empire will brief you.

224
00:16:24.985 --> 00:16:27.613
If all goes well.
you will see your husband.

225
00:16:36.288 --> 00:16:37.873
I know hope is painful.

226
00:16:39.124 --> 00:16:40.250
You don't have to hope.

227
00:16:41.043 --> 00:16:42.211
Just come with me.

228
00:17:24.086 --> 00:17:26.839
Our destination must be
on the other side of this door.

229
00:17:28.674 --> 00:17:31.760
Traditionally. doors have hinges
and maybe a knob.

230
00:17:32.636 --> 00:17:33.970
This is a wall.

231
00:17:33.971 --> 00:17:36.306
Open a wall. it becomes a door.

232
00:18:55.844 --> 00:18:58.387
I do hope the trek on the sand

233
00:18:58.388 --> 00:19:01.016
wasn't harder than you were prepared
to endure.

234
00:19:01.017 --> 00:19:02.808
I know your face.

235
00:19:02.809 --> 00:19:05.812
I've seen depictions
and I know that meter.

236
00:19:07.981 --> 00:19:09.024
You're Kalle. but...

237
00:19:10.359 --> 00:19:12.693
You died centuries ago. How are you alive?

238
00:19:12.694 --> 00:19:15.531
You can ask what that means
when we meet up again.

239
00:19:17.032 --> 00:19:20.202
If the future allows us to meet up again.

240
00:19:20.953 --> 00:19:22.120
You should go back.

241
00:19:22.996 --> 00:19:23.996
I don't understand.

242
00:19:23.997 --> 00:19:26.624
You said you couldn't venture
far from the Radiant.

243
00:19:26.625 --> 00:19:29.253
I have the means to sustain
a pure digital form.

244
00:19:29.878 --> 00:19:32.755
- He'll persist.
- Persist? What?

245
00:19:32.756 --> 00:19:37.135
I don't know what's going to happen next.
So perhaps we should say goodbye.

246
00:19:37.136 --> 00:19:41.389
If you don't hear from me
within six hours. leave.

247
00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:44.309
I've already transferred control
of the <i>Beggar</i> back to Salvor.

248
00:19:44.310 --> 00:19:45.936
Wait. don't leave!

249
00:19:48.105 --> 00:19:49.106
Fuck!

250
00:20:15.174 --> 00:20:17.217
Offered for consideration.

251
00:20:18.177 --> 00:20:20.429
Master Trader Ponyets is ready
when you are. sir.

252
00:20:25.893 --> 00:20:28.103
Open communications.

253
00:20:37.946 --> 00:20:42.075
Commdor Argo. honor be on you.

254
00:20:42.076 --> 00:20:43.242
And thank you.

255
00:20:43.243 --> 00:20:45.328
<i>Thank you for seeing me.</i>

256
00:20:45.329 --> 00:20:48.498
Ponyets. we've been warned of your kind.

257
00:20:49.249 --> 00:20:53.837
My people will take no commerce that
carries with it a compulsory religion.

258
00:20:53.838 --> 00:20:57.341
<i>No. I'm a Master Trader.
Money is my religion and</i>...

259
00:20:59.176 --> 00:21:00.344
<i>Commdor?</i>

260
00:21:00.844 --> 00:21:01.929
<i>One moment.</i>

261
00:21:03.639 --> 00:21:05.264
That's not Trader Ponyets.

262
00:21:05.265 --> 00:21:08.727
That's Hober Mallow.
a notorious confidence man.

263
00:21:10.395 --> 00:21:14.566
Forcer. I am aware he is trying
to sell me a useless device.

264
00:21:15.567 --> 00:21:17.276
Undoubtedly for half our treasury.

265
00:21:17.277 --> 00:21:20.280
I'm going to lure him in
and expose him as a cheat.

266
00:21:21.031 --> 00:21:22.366
I know what I'm doing.

267
00:21:23.784 --> 00:21:25.619
<i>Did your Forcer say I was a cheat?</i>

268
00:21:26.453 --> 00:21:29.038
<i>Yeah. she's right. All traders are cheats.</i>

269
00:21:29.039 --> 00:21:33.877
But. Your Esteem. even a cheat
can stumble across a miracle.

270
00:21:33.878 --> 00:21:36.129
You're as bold as brass. Ponyets.

271
00:21:37.005 --> 00:21:37.922
Very well.

272
00:21:37.923 --> 00:21:40.174
<i>Demonstrate your miracle.</i>

273
00:21:40.175 --> 00:21:43.219
It is called a castling device.

274
00:21:43.220 --> 00:21:48.976
And I am confident it'll earn its place
next to the Eye of Korell in your heart.

275
00:21:53.647 --> 00:21:54.940
Looks fairly ordinary.

276
00:21:55.440 --> 00:21:57.275
We've never heard of "castling."

277
00:21:57.276 --> 00:21:59.111
<i>Except in chess. of course.</i>

278
00:21:59.820 --> 00:22:01.070
Very astute.

279
00:22:01.071 --> 00:22:06.618
Yes. it is named after the chess maneuver
in which a king and a rook trade places.

280
00:22:06.619 --> 00:22:09.621
<i>A scientist
working in quantum entanglement</i>

281
00:22:09.622 --> 00:22:11.205
<i>stumbled across a mechanism</i>

282
00:22:11.206 --> 00:22:14.542
that can move a living being
over a great distance.

283
00:22:14.543 --> 00:22:17.880
as long as there's a body
of approximately equal mass

284
00:22:17.881 --> 00:22:20.507
to make the reciprocal journey.

285
00:22:20.508 --> 00:22:23.134
And you came to possess this. how?

286
00:22:23.135 --> 00:22:27.347
The scientist refused
to hand the plans over to Empire.

287
00:22:27.348 --> 00:22:29.433
She feared what would be done with it.

288
00:22:30.475 --> 00:22:34.228
You know.
moving deadly troops into civilian areas.

289
00:22:34.229 --> 00:22:37.941
<i>Sewing bombs into prisoners
and then transporting them</i>

290
00:22:37.942 --> 00:22:39.693
<i>into the middle of a demonstration.</i>

291
00:22:41.403 --> 00:22:43.550
- It's very bad.
<i>- Exactly.</i>

292
00:22:43.551 --> 00:22:45.698
I trust a principled ruler.

293
00:22:45.699 --> 00:22:47.701
such as yourself.
would use it more justly.

294
00:22:47.702 --> 00:22:48.993
<i>But is it safe?</i>

295
00:22:48.994 --> 00:22:52.038
You see. on Korell.
we've heard gruesome stories

296
00:22:52.039 --> 00:22:55.083
of men porting across planets
collapsing in agony.

297
00:22:55.084 --> 00:22:58.211
<i>No. No worries. Commdor. okay?</i>

298
00:22:58.212 --> 00:23:03.884
<i>Everything contained
in the body's bioelectrical field.</i>

299
00:23:04.468 --> 00:23:05.510
<i>travels along.</i>

300
00:23:05.511 --> 00:23:08.722
So it's just stuff outside the body
that's left behind.

301
00:23:09.431 --> 00:23:10.974
Clothes and such.

302
00:23:11.892 --> 00:23:13.227
You mean arriving naked?

303
00:23:13.228 --> 00:23:15.603
No. not naked.

304
00:23:15.604 --> 00:23:21.401
The Castler jumps
into the clothes of the other person.

305
00:23:21.944 --> 00:23:22.985
I see.

306
00:23:22.986 --> 00:23:26.782
Naturally. I have the control bracelet

307
00:23:27.449 --> 00:23:30.410
and an assistant
on the airwalk outside my ship

308
00:23:30.411 --> 00:23:31.828
has a bracelet just like yours.

309
00:23:31.829 --> 00:23:33.872
That could be faked.

310
00:23:33.873 --> 00:23:34.956
<i>Yeah.</i>

311
00:23:34.957 --> 00:23:38.355
<i>Anything can be faked.
unless it happens to you.</i>

312
00:23:38.356 --> 00:23:41.755
Well. you bothered to send a bracelet.
so use it.

313
00:23:42.631 --> 00:23:43.464
Sorry. what? I...

314
00:23:43.465 --> 00:23:45.759
You reassured us of its safety...

315
00:23:48.053 --> 00:23:50.221
- so castle me.
<i>- No... But. no. I can't.</i>

316
00:23:50.222 --> 00:23:53.933
There's rules against royalty
and commoners intermingling.

317
00:23:53.934 --> 00:23:58.480
<i>So I absolve you of them. Do it.
or I shall have your head on a pike.</i>

318
00:23:58.481 --> 00:23:59.690
If you insist.

319
00:24:09.283 --> 00:24:12.411
<i>Citizens of Korell. it's an honor.</i>

320
00:24:18.458 --> 00:24:19.584
How much do you want for it?

321
00:24:19.585 --> 00:24:21.712
<i>Yeah. it's too late. I've changed my mind.</i>

322
00:24:23.255 --> 00:24:24.255
Forcer.

323
00:24:25.674 --> 00:24:27.134
He has the Eye of Korell!

324
00:24:35.517 --> 00:24:37.060
Oh. shit.

325
00:24:43.525 --> 00:24:46.069
Hober Mallow. you're under arrest.

326
00:24:56.663 --> 00:24:58.290
You contain diamonds. Mallow.

327
00:24:58.790 --> 00:25:00.876
Yeah. To be in my bioelectrical field.

328
00:25:01.877 --> 00:25:03.586
Hey. Careful with that.

329
00:25:03.587 --> 00:25:04.983
That is a rare vintage.

330
00:25:04.984 --> 00:25:06.381
Get the device off him.

331
00:25:07.466 --> 00:25:08.466
Allow me.

332
00:25:14.598 --> 00:25:16.433
I want that wine back after the trial.

333
00:25:17.017 --> 00:25:18.227
There's no trial.

334
00:25:19.228 --> 00:25:21.563
Commdor Argo's already ordered
your execution.

335
00:25:41.416 --> 00:25:44.753
I'll escort you to Empire
when you feel that you are presentable.

336
00:25:55.556 --> 00:25:56.682
No.

337
00:26:02.020 --> 00:26:04.398
I wanna face Day like this.

338
00:26:05.107 --> 00:26:06.733
This is the man he made me.

339
00:26:12.781 --> 00:26:15.450
Thank you. Empire.

340
00:26:16.243 --> 00:26:19.037
I'm grateful to no longer be on Lepsis.

341
00:26:19.038 --> 00:26:21.248
Yes. I can smell the gratitude.

342
00:26:23.083 --> 00:26:25.459
You're here by Lady Demerzel's grace.
not mine.

343
00:26:25.460 --> 00:26:29.298
The transport that brought you here
can just as easily bring you back.

344
00:26:30.799 --> 00:26:33.260
Lady Demerzel said
that Glawen is still alive.

345
00:26:33.261 --> 00:26:36.054
- Glawen...
- Don't play games.

346
00:26:36.055 --> 00:26:38.056
He waits behind that door.

347
00:26:38.057 --> 00:26:40.057
You'll see him after we talk.

348
00:26:40.058 --> 00:26:42.477
If our talk goes well.
you'll find him alive.

349
00:26:43.562 --> 00:26:45.479
- What's the mission?
- Reconnaissance.

350
00:26:45.480 --> 00:26:48.317
- We have an informant on Siwenna.
- That's a spy's work.

351
00:26:48.318 --> 00:26:50.068
Siwenna's not a military threat.

352
00:26:51.236 --> 00:26:53.405
Not unless they're weaponizing cacti.

353
00:26:53.406 --> 00:26:55.531
So. who's your actual concern?

354
00:26:55.532 --> 00:26:59.161
Over a hundred years ago.
Hari Seldon stood where you are now.

355
00:27:00.078 --> 00:27:02.663
He claimed he could establish a Foundation

356
00:27:02.664 --> 00:27:06.125
to read the future and shorten
a coming age of darkness.

357
00:27:06.126 --> 00:27:10.881
Now I believe it was simply a ruse
to buy his people time and distance.

358
00:27:10.882 --> 00:27:13.654
Currently.
his followers worship his memory

359
00:27:13.655 --> 00:27:16.428
and recruit members
from the fringes of Empire.

360
00:27:17.179 --> 00:27:21.600
I want you to find out
if the Foundation is a threat to me.

361
00:27:25.145 --> 00:27:26.354
Can they read the future?

362
00:27:26.355 --> 00:27:29.983
That would fall under the heading
of. "Things you're supposed to find out."

363
00:27:30.859 --> 00:27:32.778
Forced labor has diminished him.

364
00:27:33.904 --> 00:27:35.342
Take him away.

365
00:27:35.343 --> 00:27:36.782
Kill the husband.

366
00:27:39.201 --> 00:27:41.578
Can I speak frankly. Empire?

367
00:27:43.413 --> 00:27:44.748
And privately.

368
00:27:45.916 --> 00:27:47.084
Just the two of us?

369
00:27:50.754 --> 00:27:52.214
Granted.

370
00:28:02.349 --> 00:28:03.684
Brothers.

371
00:28:13.360 --> 00:28:15.529
- Speak.
- You're an arrogant bully.

372
00:28:17.990 --> 00:28:22.703
If you brought me here just to kill me.
then you're an idiot as well.

373
00:28:22.704 --> 00:28:26.415
When you defied my orders in battle.
you embarrassed me.

374
00:28:27.624 --> 00:28:30.043
A man can withstand that.
but not an empire.

375
00:28:31.086 --> 00:28:35.591
An empire breathes respect.
It requires it for its life.

376
00:28:37.593 --> 00:28:40.262
It also requires planetary systems.

377
00:28:41.889 --> 00:28:45.017
And if this Foundation is picking 'em off.

378
00:28:45.767 --> 00:28:49.438
then you need the fleet
with the highest efficiency rating.

379
00:28:49.439 --> 00:28:51.607
The 20th Fleet isn't yours anymore.

380
00:28:53.483 --> 00:28:54.693
Fuck if it isn't.

381
00:28:55.819 --> 00:28:58.155
And this isn't about respect
for bloody Empire.

382
00:28:59.781 --> 00:29:01.742
I made you look foolish. didn't I?

383
00:29:02.784 --> 00:29:03.784
You.

384
00:29:03.785 --> 00:29:07.872
The singular man in that suit of skin

385
00:29:07.873 --> 00:29:10.542
that's never come within
a light-year of a battle.

386
00:29:10.543 --> 00:29:12.836
- Do you think to strike me?
- Strike ya?

387
00:29:13.629 --> 00:29:15.380
I'd like to rip your fucking head off.

388
00:29:16.757 --> 00:29:20.177
- Go ahead!
- I took an oath. you're my Emperor.

389
00:29:22.429 --> 00:29:23.846
- Strike me.
- No.

390
00:29:23.847 --> 00:29:26.641
- Strike me or I kill your husband.
- Another game?

391
00:29:26.642 --> 00:29:29.206
What answer am I looking for?
Do I want you to strike me

392
00:29:29.207 --> 00:29:31.771
so I know I can control you
by threatening your husband.

393
00:29:31.772 --> 00:29:36.193
or do I want you to refrain. to show
that you will protect Empire at all cost?

394
00:29:36.194 --> 00:29:38.987
One of these choices buys you everything.

395
00:29:39.571 --> 00:29:42.491
One sends you back to the mines a widower.

396
00:29:42.492 --> 00:29:43.909
I took an oath.

397
00:29:45.827 --> 00:29:47.746
I'll not strike my Emperor.

398
00:29:48.997 --> 00:29:50.666
Not even for Glawen's life?

399
00:29:52.668 --> 00:29:55.337
I've had a dead husband
for the last six years.

400
00:30:32.833 --> 00:30:34.168
Glawen?

401
00:30:34.710 --> 00:30:35.711
Yes?

402
00:30:41.508 --> 00:30:42.885
It's me.

403
00:30:55.856 --> 00:30:57.024
Bel?

404
00:31:00.485 --> 00:31:01.695
They brought me here...

405
00:31:04.114 --> 00:31:05.234
I thought it meant you died.

406
00:31:05.782 --> 00:31:06.992
They told me...

407
00:31:09.661 --> 00:31:11.371
They told me you had died.

408
00:31:12.748 --> 00:31:15.667
- Six years ago.
- Bel. I tried to get a message out to you.

409
00:31:15.668 --> 00:31:18.587
- They said they'd kill you if I tried.
- It's all right.

410
00:31:18.588 --> 00:31:20.505
It's all right. Glay.

411
00:31:20.506 --> 00:31:22.341
Those fucking cruel bastards.

412
00:31:23.884 --> 00:31:25.135
Watch your words.

413
00:31:26.720 --> 00:31:28.430
We're back in their service now.

414
00:31:29.890 --> 00:31:31.767
Not to mention their palace.

415
00:31:31.768 --> 00:31:32.976
In service?

416
00:31:36.480 --> 00:31:38.106
That hair is not regulation.

417
00:31:54.915 --> 00:31:56.041
No. I...

418
00:31:57.709 --> 00:32:00.796
I'm still 713.

419
00:32:02.631 --> 00:32:03.674
I'm filthy.

420
00:32:04.675 --> 00:32:06.009
My teeth...

421
00:32:09.638 --> 00:32:10.764
I've got lice.

422
00:32:54.725 --> 00:32:55.726
It's okay.

423
00:33:14.786 --> 00:33:15.954
Hey.

424
00:33:26.340 --> 00:33:27.799
I'm so sorry.

425
00:33:45.901 --> 00:33:46.902
There you are.

426
00:33:48.570 --> 00:33:49.571
Yeah.

427
00:33:51.657 --> 00:33:52.658
That's me.

428
00:34:02.668 --> 00:34:04.711
So that was the right answer?

429
00:34:05.295 --> 00:34:06.421
I don't know.

430
00:34:08.090 --> 00:34:11.592
I looked into his eyes.
and he seemed like a strong person.

431
00:34:14.929 --> 00:34:16.888
There we go.

432
00:34:16.889 --> 00:34:19.476
You wanted someone who wouldn't vacillate.

433
00:34:20.268 --> 00:34:25.107
Someone who will make a choice
and assert it. That's a good policy.

434
00:34:25.690 --> 00:34:31.071
I let go of good policy
or genetic sense memory of good policy.

435
00:34:35.242 --> 00:34:37.286
Do you know how lucky we are to have you?

436
00:34:38.078 --> 00:34:39.204
You're fine.

437
00:34:40.873 --> 00:34:42.331
You're doing well.

438
00:34:44.376 --> 00:34:45.960
You are Empire.

439
00:34:47.920 --> 00:34:48.922
Keep going.

440
00:35:17.868 --> 00:35:20.078
<i>I'm telling you. she felt alive.</i>

441
00:35:22.039 --> 00:35:25.167
But Kalle.
the real one died centuries ago.

442
00:35:26.627 --> 00:35:28.837
I have no idea
what's in that cave with him.

443
00:35:29.796 --> 00:35:30.964
Something is off.

444
00:35:31.965 --> 00:35:33.300
This whole planet is wrong.

445
00:35:34.468 --> 00:35:36.053
Six hours is almost up.

446
00:35:36.803 --> 00:35:38.055
Then we'll leave him behind.

447
00:35:38.555 --> 00:35:39.765
We have every reason to.

448
00:35:41.558 --> 00:35:42.559
I know we do.

449
00:35:44.520 --> 00:35:47.940
He's not Hari. He's a digital simulacrum.

450
00:35:48.607 --> 00:35:50.566
And he was trapped
for over a hundred years.

451
00:35:50.567 --> 00:35:53.153
Even he said that kind of isolation
can drive someone mad.

452
00:35:53.154 --> 00:35:55.697
It's not me that needs convincing.

453
00:35:57.741 --> 00:36:01.370
Look. whatever version of Hari this is...

454
00:36:03.789 --> 00:36:04.998
he scares me.

455
00:36:07.543 --> 00:36:08.961
And the two of you together...

456
00:36:11.296 --> 00:36:15.467
Gaal. he almost suffocated you.

457
00:36:15.468 --> 00:36:17.553
And you encouraged it.

458
00:36:19.304 --> 00:36:23.934
So if you say. "Fly us out of here."
I will take us right up.

459
00:36:26.270 --> 00:36:27.271
But?

460
00:36:28.105 --> 00:36:30.566
But I don't think you want that.

461
00:36:37.114 --> 00:36:39.074
You and him. you got your own language.

462
00:36:42.077 --> 00:36:43.161
I don't speak it.

463
00:36:48.500 --> 00:36:50.043
Look. all I'm saying is...

464
00:36:52.421 --> 00:36:54.464
you're more like him
than you want to admit.

465
00:36:56.967 --> 00:36:58.177
Maybe you're right.

466
00:37:00.304 --> 00:37:01.722
He was my idol.

467
00:37:03.182 --> 00:37:05.642
Father figure I convinced myself I needed.

468
00:37:06.977 --> 00:37:08.979
Yeah. that's the thing with parents.
isn't it?

469
00:37:08.980 --> 00:37:11.106
Never quite who you build them up to be.

470
00:37:17.112 --> 00:37:18.405
My dad used to say...

471
00:37:20.532 --> 00:37:24.578
"Never let your sense of morals
prevent you from doing what's right."

472
00:37:25.871 --> 00:37:27.456
So just ask yourself. Gaal.

473
00:37:28.081 --> 00:37:32.002
if the situation were reversed.
what would Hari do now?

474
00:37:40.093 --> 00:37:41.303
He'd fucking leave.

475
00:38:03.909 --> 00:38:06.328
Wonder what's going on?
Some kind of celebration?

476
00:38:06.329 --> 00:38:12.125
First prisoner death by Titan's prick.

477
00:38:12.668 --> 00:38:14.711
Go!

478
00:38:16.672 --> 00:38:20.467
Yeah!

479
00:38:23.887 --> 00:38:25.450
Bring the next one!

480
00:38:25.451 --> 00:38:27.015
Second prisoner.

481
00:38:29.810 --> 00:38:31.081
- Hober Mallow.
- Boo!

482
00:38:31.082 --> 00:38:33.073
- Boo!
- Fuck. no!

483
00:38:33.074 --> 00:38:35.065
Death by Titan's prick!

484
00:38:35.649 --> 00:38:37.192
Hober Mallow!

485
00:38:39.278 --> 00:38:41.029
- Hober!
- Hello.

486
00:38:41.030 --> 00:38:42.613
Yeah!

487
00:38:42.614 --> 00:38:44.031
I'm rather busy right now.

488
00:38:44.032 --> 00:38:49.162
Shut up. you ass. We've come to free you.
The Foundation needs you.

489
00:38:49.163 --> 00:38:52.415
The Vault opened yesterday.
it requested your presence.

490
00:38:52.416 --> 00:38:55.669
Poly Verisof.
I've never met a man with worse timing!

491
00:38:59.298 --> 00:39:00.299
Forcer Wallick.

492
00:39:01.425 --> 00:39:03.802
I hate to dampen your enthusiasm.
but apparently.

493
00:39:03.803 --> 00:39:06.180
something's come up
and the Foundation needs me.

494
00:39:06.181 --> 00:39:08.599
So. if you could just not execute me?

495
00:39:10.559 --> 00:39:11.685
Not listening. Poly.

496
00:39:12.853 --> 00:39:15.606
You with the Claric? Hilarious. isn't he?

497
00:39:16.356 --> 00:39:19.610
Stories I could tell you
if my capital wasn't about to be punished.

498
00:39:24.323 --> 00:39:25.908
Forcer Wallick. is this your design?

499
00:39:26.491 --> 00:39:28.577
Very efficient. Cozy.

500
00:39:32.998 --> 00:39:33.999
Your Esteem.

501
00:39:34.666 --> 00:39:38.837
I ask that you allow me
to meet with Hober in private.

502
00:39:39.379 --> 00:39:42.673
before he faces the prospect
of going unprepared

503
00:39:42.674 --> 00:39:45.969
into the bosom of
the great Galactic Spirit.

504
00:39:46.720 --> 00:39:50.139
You are a tender of the soul?

505
00:39:50.140 --> 00:39:52.559
One of the Foundation's so-called Clarics?

506
00:39:52.560 --> 00:39:54.937
I have been so trained.

507
00:39:56.939 --> 00:40:02.236
Every man should prepare his soul before
journeying to the ancestral spirits.

508
00:40:02.237 --> 00:40:07.866
Alas. you will have
to prepare Hober's posthumously.

509
00:40:07.867 --> 00:40:10.702
- Death by Titan's prick!
- No. no!

510
00:40:14.831 --> 00:40:16.999
Stop this at once. damn it!

511
00:40:17.000 --> 00:40:19.545
In the name of the Galactic Spirit.
we submit ourselves.

512
00:40:23.423 --> 00:40:28.178
Your Esteem. death is so irrevocable
a phenomenon. Surely...

513
00:40:28.929 --> 00:40:31.056
Come on. there must be an alternative?

514
00:40:31.057 --> 00:40:33.350
Alas. no.

515
00:40:37.980 --> 00:40:41.733
But thank you for the parting gifts.
Master Trader.

516
00:40:43.652 --> 00:40:45.904
I shall enjoy the wine this evening.

517
00:40:45.905 --> 00:40:47.698
Say your last words. fool.

518
00:40:48.282 --> 00:40:49.867
Citizens of Korell.

519
00:40:51.410 --> 00:40:58.125
I was born of modest means.
and I faced many obstacles in my life.

520
00:40:59.334 --> 00:41:05.090
I suppose it's not the past I should
dwell on. but the future I'll be denied.

521
00:41:06.258 --> 00:41:08.844
The acts of charity I'll never carry out.

522
00:41:10.345 --> 00:41:11.513
The strangers...

523
00:41:13.932 --> 00:41:15.183
I'll never meet.

524
00:41:15.184 --> 00:41:19.646
Enemies I might have charmed into friends.

525
00:41:21.148 --> 00:41:23.942
But it's not to be.

526
00:41:24.526 --> 00:41:28.322
I played my game too boldly
and I see that now.

527
00:41:30.699 --> 00:41:36.038
And here I am. I have no move
that will not put me in check.

528
00:41:36.039 --> 00:41:37.560
- Enough!
- And I...

529
00:41:37.561 --> 00:41:39.082
Drop the prick on him!

530
00:41:39.583 --> 00:41:41.877
Well. actually. I hadn't finished.

531
00:41:42.377 --> 00:41:44.213
I hadn't finished! I've just wa...

532
00:41:56.099 --> 00:41:59.018
Hey! Fuck is going on?

533
00:41:59.019 --> 00:42:02.356
Fucking get me out of here.
I am not Hober Mallow.

534
00:42:02.357 --> 00:42:04.858
It's the Commdor! Stop the prick!

535
00:42:06.443 --> 00:42:08.612
Hober Mallow. you fuck!

536
00:42:13.825 --> 00:42:15.952
Sleight of hand. Your Esteem.

537
00:42:15.953 --> 00:42:19.540
It was this node. not the bracelet.
that did the switch.

538
00:42:19.541 --> 00:42:22.626
- Poly. always a pleasure.
- Well. stop him!

539
00:42:27.089 --> 00:42:29.132
Wow. He's very confident.

540
00:42:29.925 --> 00:42:31.176
He's appalling.

541
00:42:31.885 --> 00:42:34.429
- How far can he get on an air yacht?
- Alert the spaceports!

542
00:42:34.430 --> 00:42:37.474
He knows that we've got a jumpship.
He's gonna take it!

543
00:42:38.350 --> 00:42:40.102
He's gonna take the <i>Spirit</i>!

544
00:42:56.827 --> 00:42:59.329
Come on. up! Up!

545
00:43:00.163 --> 00:43:01.415
Constant!

546
00:43:21.101 --> 00:43:24.124
Welcome. Exciting. isn't it?
I'm gonna need your personal access codes.

547
00:43:24.125 --> 00:43:26.956
We're not jumping to whatever
lawless zone you set your coordinates to.

548
00:43:26.957 --> 00:43:29.789
What? You'd rather they shoot us down?
You're better off jumping...

549
00:43:30.402 --> 00:43:31.612
Keep him away from me.

550
00:43:33.739 --> 00:43:34.739
Hello.

551
00:43:34.740 --> 00:43:36.240
Drop me off on the nearest asteroid.

552
00:43:36.241 --> 00:43:38.911
- We need you on Terminus.
- I'm not going to Terminus.

553
00:43:40.370 --> 00:43:43.457
Would you keep her quiet?
I'm trying to pilot.

554
00:43:50.547 --> 00:43:51.881
You're not taking the escape pod.

555
00:43:51.882 --> 00:43:54.602
Look. if you think I won't hurt you
because you're a woman. I will...

556
00:43:55.135 --> 00:43:57.179
What is that? You stabbing me.
is that supposed...

557
00:44:00.015 --> 00:44:01.475
What was...

558
00:44:03.310 --> 00:44:04.311
That's it.

559
00:44:05.854 --> 00:44:07.022
Get it all out.

560
00:44:24.039 --> 00:44:25.749
You got everything you wanted.

561
00:44:28.752 --> 00:44:30.045
We could disappear.

562
00:44:34.049 --> 00:44:36.343
Empire has been monstrous to you. Bel.

563
00:44:37.719 --> 00:44:39.345
He's been monstrous to me.

564
00:44:39.346 --> 00:44:40.972
That's why we can't just run.

565
00:44:40.973 --> 00:44:43.558
A weak Emperor needs a strong general.

566
00:44:43.559 --> 00:44:46.144
And he'll be fearful of that general.

567
00:44:47.062 --> 00:44:48.813
He'll always be imagining a coup.

568
00:44:48.814 --> 00:44:52.025
He didn't imprison you
because of some order you disobeyed.

569
00:44:52.026 --> 00:44:53.902
he did it because you are loved.

570
00:44:53.903 --> 00:44:55.028
It's immaterial.

571
00:44:56.071 --> 00:45:01.034
I'm not a revolutionary. Glawen.
any more than I am a deserter.

572
00:45:03.620 --> 00:45:06.707
The Emperor's subjects. all these
trillions of people. they're just...

573
00:45:07.916 --> 00:45:09.543
they're disposable to him.

574
00:45:11.753 --> 00:45:16.008
So. as the one man who isn't.
it's my duty to protect them. Glay.

575
00:45:17.217 --> 00:45:18.844
- All of them.
- Right now?

576
00:45:20.262 --> 00:45:22.181
Bel. you need time to recover.

577
00:45:22.681 --> 00:45:26.727
And we need time to find each other again.

578
00:45:28.228 --> 00:45:30.230
I'll be by your side. no matter what.

579
00:45:30.231 --> 00:45:31.356
But I tell you.

580
00:45:32.774 --> 00:45:37.029
being under Empire's heel leaves a mark.

581
00:45:38.030 --> 00:45:40.177
And that doesn't go away
when the heel is lifted.

582
00:45:40.178 --> 00:45:42.326
So. you're gonna be at my side
every minute. are you?

583
00:45:42.910 --> 00:45:44.620
Looking for the tread marks on my face.

584
00:45:46.288 --> 00:45:47.664
They're not on your face.

585
00:45:54.713 --> 00:45:57.883
<i>Approaching Destiny.
Prepare the cabin for docking.</i>

586
00:46:00.636 --> 00:46:01.637
The point remains.

587
00:46:03.430 --> 00:46:05.390
With this Day in charge.

588
00:46:06.433 --> 00:46:08.143
for the sake of all these people.

589
00:46:09.770 --> 00:46:12.105
I don't have the luxury
of settling the score.

590
00:46:13.941 --> 00:46:20.155
I was prepared for you to say that.
which is why I kept this for you.

591
00:46:25.077 --> 00:46:26.245
General.

592
00:47:22.968 --> 00:47:23.969
At ease.

593
00:47:28.390 --> 00:47:30.057
Welcome home. General Riose.

594
00:47:30.058 --> 00:47:32.186
It's good to be back. She-Bends-Light.

595
00:47:37.107 --> 00:47:39.109
I hope.
during your years under gravity's boot.

596
00:47:39.110 --> 00:47:40.986
you haven't forgotten how to space-fold.

597
00:47:42.237 --> 00:47:44.907
We didn't pack any sick bags
for this journey.

598
00:47:47.284 --> 00:47:50.204
- Missed your humor. She-Bends.
- And I your smile. General.

599
00:47:51.205 --> 00:47:52.872
All those years opalesk mining.

600
00:47:52.873 --> 00:47:55.918
and you still only brought me
remnants under your fingernails.

601
00:47:57.252 --> 00:47:58.837
I'm teasing. General.

602
00:47:59.463 --> 00:48:02.466
Empire couldn't control my kind
if they didn't keep a stranglehold on it.

603
00:48:03.634 --> 00:48:05.427
Set a course for the Outer Reach.

604
00:48:13.727 --> 00:48:15.395
It's not too late to belay that.

605
00:48:16.355 --> 00:48:17.773
Jump locked in.

606
00:48:18.524 --> 00:48:19.608
Too late now.

607
00:48:20.484 --> 00:48:22.236
All hands to jump creches.

608
00:48:46.426 --> 00:48:49.471
Fine. We'll build a Second Foundation
without Hari.

609
00:48:51.765 --> 00:48:53.183
Takeoff might be a little rough.

610
00:49:05.946 --> 00:49:07.990
<i>Warning. Planetary surface thin.</i>

611
00:49:07.991 --> 00:49:09.448
- You all right?
- Yeah.

612
00:49:09.449 --> 00:49:11.910
<i>- Landing site unstable.</i>
- Yeah. thanks.

613
00:49:11.911 --> 00:49:13.161
It's all right. We'll just...

614
00:49:17.541 --> 00:49:19.042
Oh. shit.

615
00:49:20.794 --> 00:49:22.629
Uninhabited doesn't mean alone.

616
00:49:32.055 --> 00:49:34.933
- Get us out of here! Fly us out!
- Yes. I'm trying. I'm trying!

617
00:49:46.195 --> 00:49:47.738
Watch out!

618
00:49:52.868 --> 00:49:54.368
Come on.

619
00:49:54.369 --> 00:49:55.954
Nearly there.

620
00:50:10.052 --> 00:50:11.762
What the hell were those?

621
00:50:12.888 --> 00:50:13.888
Did we lose 'em?

622
00:50:13.889 --> 00:50:17.768
No. They just turned around. It's like
they got a scent of something else.

623
00:50:19.561 --> 00:50:22.022
Not possible.
There's nothing alive on this rock but us.

624
00:50:30.364 --> 00:50:31.365
Wait.

625
00:50:33.534 --> 00:50:36.620
Probes are picking up activity
in those monuments.

626
00:50:36.621 --> 00:50:37.704
What?

627
00:50:38.288 --> 00:50:39.289
A life-form.

628
00:50:39.790 --> 00:50:41.834
Maybe that Kalle person was alive.

629
00:50:42.417 --> 00:50:44.086
There's something breathing down there.

630
00:50:48.131 --> 00:50:49.382
It's Hari.

631
00:50:49.383 --> 00:50:50.842
What? No. it can't be Hari.

632
00:50:50.843 --> 00:50:53.595
I'm telling you. it's him. It's Hari.

633
00:50:55.848 --> 00:50:56.931
Turn.

634
00:50:56.932 --> 00:50:58.454
There's nowhere to land.

635
00:50:58.455 --> 00:50:59.977
Bring us down onto the hand.

636
00:51:25.711 --> 00:51:27.087
Open the air lock.

637
00:51:49.651 --> 00:51:51.278
You have to fly closer!

638
00:52:02.164 --> 00:52:03.519
I've got a pulse. Salvor.

639
00:52:03.520 --> 00:52:04.875
<i>He's real. He's alive.</i>

640
00:52:09.296 --> 00:52:10.672
What are you?

641
00:52:24.353 --> 00:52:27.356
Gaal. hurry. Those things are gonna
take down the entire mountain.

642
00:52:36.573 --> 00:52:38.075
You have to wake up.

643
00:52:42.663 --> 00:52:44.957
Salvor. pull us up!

644
00:52:44.958 --> 00:52:46.625
Hang on!

645
00:53:00.973 --> 00:53:03.225
Hari. wake up. Come on.

646
00:53:03.226 --> 00:53:04.309
Wake up.

647
00:53:08.730 --> 00:53:12.067
How do you have a body?
How is this possible?

648
00:53:14.278 --> 00:53:15.279
I don't know.

649
00:53:16.305 --> 00:54:16.818
